2. Triton fused-attention tutorial (MIT) -- precautionary
---------------------------------------------------------

src/tether/accel/kernels/attention.py implements the online-softmax
(FlashAttention-style) recurrence with the same idioms as Triton's MIT-licensed
tutorial python/tutorials/06-fused-attention.py (running max ``m_i``, running
sum ``l_i``, ``qk_scale = scale * log2(e)`` with ``exp2``). The upstream file
carries no derivation notice and its structure (grouped-query row folding,
device-resident key length, split-KV with fused FP8 output) differs from the
tutorial, so derivation is UNKNOWN. The MIT notice is reproduced here in case
